    <string name="guide_body1">GST is the tax on the sale of goods and services in India. When buyer and seller are in the same state, the bill shows CGST + SGST. When they are in different states, the bill shows IGST. The rate depends on the item — check its HSN code.</string>
    <string name="guide_body2">GST rates in this app: 0%, 5%, 12%, 18% and 28% (plus 0.1%, 0.25%, 1.5% and 3% for special items like gold). Everyday food items are often 0% or 5%; most general goods are 12% or 18%. The correct rate comes from the item\'s HSN code — when in doubt, ask your CA.</string>
    <string name="guide_body3">GSTR-1 lists the sales (outward supplies) of the month. GSTR-3B is the monthly summary — total sales, total tax, and the tax you pay. Both are filed on the GST portal; this app only prepares draft reports. Due dates change — always check the GST portal for the current month\'s dates.</string>
    <string name="guide_body4">e-Invoice means a B2B invoice gets an IRN (Invoice Reference Number) from the portal, with a QR code. e-Way Bill is needed to move goods from one place to another. Both apply only above certain turnover limits — check the GST portal for the current limits before you rely on them.</string>
    <string name="guide_body5">GSTR-9 is the annual return — a summary of the whole financial year. It is mandatory when yearly turnover is above Rs 2 crore. If your turnover is below that, check the portal — the rule can change.</string>
    <string name="guide_body6">Common mistakes: (1) wrong GSTIN on the bill, (2) wrong state — CGST + SGST shown for an inter-state sale, or IGST for an intra-state sale, (3) claiming ITC without checking GSTR-2B on the portal, (4) treating this app\'s draft report as a filed return — filing happens only on the GST portal, (5) a credit note saved as a normal bill.</string>
    <string name="guide_hint">ছোট, সহজ তথ্য। ফাইলিং ও শেষ তারিখের জন্য সবসময় GST পোর্টাল দেখুন।</string>
